*** Add File:docs/runbooks/bigdata_runbook.md
+# Big Data Runbook (EMR / Dataproc / Delta / Iceberg)
+
+1) Choose managed Spark offering that fits your org:
+   - AWS: EMR Serverless or EMR on EC2 (EMR Serverless recommended for ad-hoc ETL)
+   - GCP: Dataproc
+   - Azure: Databricks or Synapse for enterprise usability
+
+2) Storage & catalog:
+   - Object store: S3 / GCS / ADLS
+   - Catalog: AWS Glue (Delta), Hive metastore, or Iceberg catalog (Hadoop / S3)
+
+3) ETL patterns:
+   - Ingest raw -> landing bucket -> Spark transform -> write to Delta/Iceberg -> optimize & vacuum
+   - For streaming ingestion consider Structured Streaming + Kafka / Kinesis
+
+4) Embedding pipeline:
+   - Run batch jobs to compute embeddings and push vectors to Milvus for RAG
+   - Ensure idempotent ingestion (use record ids) to allow re-run without duplication
+
+5) Monitoring:
+   - Use Cloud provider job monitoring + Prometheus exporters
+   - Track job durations, failure rates, shuffle size and executor memory
+
+6) Security:
+   - Use cluster IAM roles / short-lived tokens and Vault for secrets
+   - Enable encryption at rest for S3 / buckets
+
